{"ref":"BDB, מִשְׁלַח","hw":"מִשְׁלַח","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מִשְׁלַח</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>1. outstretching</strong>; <strong>2. place of letting loose</strong>:—<span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> only cstr.:<br><strong>1.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּכָל־מ׳ יַד פ׳</span> <em>in every outstretching of</em> one’s <em>hand</em>, = every understaking, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.7\">Dt 12:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 12:18\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.12.18\">18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 15:10\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.15.10\">15:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 23:21\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.23.21\">23:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.8\">28:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 28:20\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.28.20\">20</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <span dir=\"rtl\">לְמ׳ שׁוֹר וּלְמִרְמֶס שֶׂה</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 7:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.7.25\">Is 7:25</a> (√ <strong>Pi. 3</strong> especially <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 32:20\" href=\"/Isaiah.32.20\">Is 32:20</a>).","next":"BDB, מִשְׁלוֹחַ","prev":"BDB, שְׁלוּחָה"}